<article class="env-lemma" id="017D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/017D">Lemma <span data-tag="017D">14.13.2</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category such that the coproduct of any two objects of $\mathcal{C}$ exists. Let $U$ be a simplicial set. Let $V$ be a simplicial object of $\mathcal{C}$. Assume that each $U_ n$ is finite nonempty. The functor $W \mapsto \mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits _{\text{Simp}(\mathcal{C})}(U \times V, W)$ is canonically isomorphic to the functor which maps $W$ to the set in Equation (<a href="/tag/017B" data-tag="017B">14.13.0.1</a>). </p>
